.TH YUME-GUI 1 "2026-06-27" "YUME 1.1" "YUME Manual"
.SH NAME
yume-gui \- desktop UI for the YUME post-quantum stealth transport
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yume-gui
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yume-gui
is an optional Dear ImGui desktop application. It embeds the same
facade sessions used by automation and tests: a
.BR yumed (8)
server controller and a linked, in-process
.BR yume (1)
client runtime.
.PP
The GUI does not reimplement the transport stack. JSON profiles written
here are compatible with the CLI binaries.
.SH WORKSPACES
The sidebar switches between two workspaces:
.TP
.B Client
Connect, security, logs, settings, and credits for the
.BR yume (1)
runtime.
.TP
.B Server
Server control, authorized keys, logs, settings, and credits for
.BR yumed (8).
.SH PAGES
.TP
.B Dashboard
Connection summary and quick status for the active workspace.
.TP
.B Connect
Server host, identity key, SOCKS port, stealth toggles, and connect /
disconnect controls.
.TP
.B Security
Inner crypto, TLS profile, obfs secret, and trust material (CA pins,
operator CA import; the historical config identifier remains compatible).
.TP
.B Server
Listen port, TLS cert paths, auth keys, real HTTP facade, and daemon
start/stop.
.TP
.B Keys
Generate composite Ed25519 + ML-DSA-87 identities and manage
.B authorized_keys
entries.
.TP
.B Logs
Live log view for the embedded client or server session.
.TP
.B Settings
Appearance (theme), paths, and runtime preferences.
.TP
.B Credits
Project version and license notice.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --headless
Run a no-window smoke test of the embedded facade. Exits after
verifying that client and server sessions initialize. Useful on CI
hosts without a display server.
.TP
.B --start-minimized
Open hidden. Use the tray menu (when available) to show the main
window.
.TP
.B --no-tray
Disable the system tray icon at runtime even when the build includes
tray support.
.TP
.BI "--client-config " path
Load the client JSON profile from
.I path
instead of the platform default.
.TP
.BI "--server-config " path
Load the server JSON profile from
.I path
instead of the platform default.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print a help summary and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD AND WINDOW
.PP
Standard Dear ImGui navigation applies: click fields to edit, Tab to
move focus, Enter to activate buttons. The main window can be resized;
the sidebar layout adapts to narrow widths.
.PP
There is no global accelerator table yet. Use the sidebar to switch
pages.
.SH SYSTEM TRAY
When tray support is compiled in and not disabled with
.BR --no-tray ,
a status icon may appear in the desktop environment's notification
area.
.PP
On Wayland (KDE Plasma, GNOME with certain compositors), tray behavior
depends on the desktop portal and StatusNotifier implementation. If the
icon is missing, run with
.B --no-tray
and keep the main window visible, or use the CLI binaries directly.
.SH BUILD
The GUI is optional:
.PP
.nf
cmake -B build -DYUME_BUILD_GUI=ON
cmake --build build -j$(nproc)
.fi
.PP
Requires OpenGL, GLFW, and ImGui/ImPlot fetched by CMake. Debian
packaging skips the GUI when
.B DEB_BUILD_PROFILES
contains
.BR nogui .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.yume/client.json
Default GUI client profile (Linux). macOS and Windows use the
platform-specific config directory under the user home.
.TP
.I ~/.yume/server.json
Default GUI server configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.yume/secure-materials/
Imported operator CAs and client auth keys managed by the Security page.
.TP
.I ~/.yume/keys/
Default key generation directory.
